.TH SDL_GetJoystickAxisInitialState 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetJoystickAxisInitialState \- Get the initial state of an axis control on a joystick.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_joystick.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetJoystickAxisInitialState(SDL_Joystick *joystick, int axis, Sint16 *state);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The state is a value ranging from -32768 to 32767\[char46]
.PP
The axis indices start at index 0\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I joystick
an
.BR SDL_Joystick
structure containing joystick information\[char46]
.TP
.I axis
the axis to query; the axis indices start at index 0\[char46]
.TP
.I state
upon return, the initial value is supplied here\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if this axis has any initial value, or false if not\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

